; Tzar2 engine default skirmish AI.
; Written for Tzar2 (MIT licence); it is not part of the original game. The game uses the original scripts of the
; player's own install (DATA/AI, imported into the base package); this script runs when they are missing, in tests and
; in benchmarks. It is written in the legacy AI language (docs/tdd/D-legacy-ai-dsl.md) and names only the object
; classes of the M2/M3 classic subset, so it also documents what the interpreter understands.

rule say "Tzar2 default AI ready" forget THIS end

; ---- housing: keep room for the next units
; (thresholds derived for this script: the castle's room plus about one house per eight to twelve units, rounded so
;  that a house is started before the room runs out; not taken from any original table)
{ critical rule when castle 1 end
  rule when units 18 have 1 house end
  rule when units 26 have 2 houses end
  rule when units 34 have 4 houses end
  rule when units 44 have 6 houses end
  rule when units 58 have 9 houses end
  rule when units 76 have 12 houses end
  rule when units 100 have 16 houses end
  rule when units 130 have 20 houses end
}

; ---- the town
rule have castle end
{ critical rule when castle 1 end
  rule have 10 peons end
  rule when units 16 have 16 peons end
  rule when units 30 have 22 peons end
  rule when units 50 have 28 peons end
  rule when difficulty hard have 40% peons end
  rule when not difficulty hard have 30% peons end
  rule when peons 6 have farm end
  rule when peons 9 have lumber end
  rule when peons 12 have storage end
}

; ---- hard: save stone for the second barracks (what follows may not spend it until 400 are stocked)
{ critical rule when difficulty hard, barracks, not barracks 2 end
  rule have 400 stone end
  rule have needs_locked end
}

; ---- a first guard, then barracks
{ critical rule when castle, peons 8 end
  critical rule have 1 barracks end
  rule have 6 footmen end
  rule have 4 archers end
  rule when footmen 6 trigger Guarded end
}
rule when trigger Guarded say "My town is guarded" forget THIS end

; ---- the army grows with the economy
{ critical rule when trigger Guarded end
  rule when peons 16 have 2 barracks end
  rule have 12 footmen end
  rule have 8 archers end
  rule have 6 macemen end
  rule when units 50 have 20% footmen end
  rule when units 50 have 15% archers end
  rule when units 70 have 10% macemen end
  rule when knight have 10 knights end
}

; ---- what each civilization trains best
{ critical rule when trigger Guarded end
  rule when civ european, barracks 2 have 10 pikemen end
  rule when civ arabian, barracks 2 have 10 pikemen end
  rule when civ arabian have 8 heavy_cavalry end
  rule when civ asian have 8 horse_samurai end
}

; ---- answer what the enemy brings
rule trigger !FacingCavalry end
rule when enemy knights 8 trigger FacingCavalry end
rule when enemy heavy_cavalry 8 trigger FacingCavalry end
rule when trigger FacingCavalry, civ european have 16 pikemen end
rule when trigger FacingCavalry, civ asian have 16 macemen end
